AIKIDO-2026-310861 (CWE-843) — seroval-plugins: pin the vulnerable seroval core
dependency to the fixed release.

The vulnerability lives in the seroval CORE package
(packages/seroval/src/core/context/deserializer.ts): a crafted serialized payload
could make a deserialized Promise fulfillment/rejection value be itself thenable,
hijacking the Promise resolution chain. Upstream fixed it in seroval 1.6.2
(commit f1ffcc96d259f9b5b3d71feb262b58240c90e7b7) by adding an isThennable()
guard that throws SerovalMalformedNodeError.

The published seroval-plugins@1.5.6 npm artifact ships only web/*.ts plugin
sources and dist/ output — it does NOT contain deserializer.ts. seroval-plugins
consumes the vulnerable code exclusively through its `seroval` dependency
(declared as a peer dependency). The only artifact-applicable remediation for
this package is therefore to raise the dependency constraint so that installs
resolve a fixed seroval core (>= 1.6.2), and to bump the pinned dev dependency
used to build/test the package. This patch targets package.json, which is
present at the tarball root (package/package.json) and applies cleanly at -p1.

--- a/package.json
+++ b/package.json
@@ -17,13 +17,13 @@
     "@types/node": "^24.10.0",
     "@vitest/ui": "^4.0.6",
     "pridepack": "2.6.4",
-    "seroval": "1.5.6",
+    "seroval": "1.6.2",
     "tslib": "^2.8.1",
     "typescript": "^5.9.3",
     "vitest": "^4.0.6"
   },
   "peerDependencies": {
-    "seroval": "^1.0"
+    "seroval": "^1.6.2"
   },
   "private": false,
   "description": "Stringify JS values",
